From: macmanes <macmanes@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 18:05:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] Reproducible hash codes for identity-compared hash keys

SimpleEdge, Path, PathWithOrig, PathOverlap, SimplePathNodeEdge,
Path_n_MM_count, AlignmentStats and My_DFS are HashMap/HashSet keys
(jung keys its edge maps by SimpleEdge) but had no hashCode, so map order
followed the JVM's identity hash. That hash is handed out in request order,
so any code path that asked for one first, such as Object.toString in a
debug message, changed the assembly.

Hash a per-instance creation counter through a mixing function instead:
deterministic, and random-like as the identity hash was. (Plain creation
order also made runs reproducible but moved total assembled bases by
several percent, so the order matters to Butterfly.) equals stays identity.
